<title>GREECE: INTEREST ON GREEK BONDS TO BE AUCTIONED NOV 22 IS TAX FREE - MIN.</title>
<headline>INTEREST ON GREEK BONDS TO BE AUCTIONED NOV 22 IS TAX FREE - MIN.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest on Greek bonds to be auctioned on November 22 is tax free, the finance ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>There has been a lot of market speculation lately as to whether the government will tax interest on outstanding FRNs and bonds but government officials have refused to speak out on the taxation issue.</p>
<p>The same statement contained basic information on the auction of seven-year floaters and three-year fixed coupon bonds to be auctioned next Friday.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
